Acceptance criteria:
  The new mission is background and unstarted on new and compatible old workspaces;
    no existing primary mission, modes, checkpoint, evidence or dates are rewritten.
  The roadmap covers discovery, engineering/data/integration, responsible AI,
    production operations, adoption, handoff, product feedback and interview proof.
  Author-created sequence and criteria are distinguished from employer requirements.
  Sources expose reviewed scope, vendor-specific assumptions and unstable job listings.
  No paid account, real customer data or unsupervised production access is mandatory.
  All existing mission-supporting views recognize the new stable identity.
  The graph explains real cross-mission transfer without granting equivalent credit.
  Atlas remains the same finite collection, deriving recognition from FDE evidence
    and eligible recall; no separate score, reset or fabricated professional rank.
  Old schema-one/two backups and encrypted journal chains retain actual records.
  Invalid FDE data fails explicitly; missing old data is not treated as corruption.
  Technical completion, human acceptance and exact-source publication stay separate.

